   "note": "Scope point, described as a waveform and never as a level. §2-161 has U3B subtracting U3A's half wave from the H4 signal to leave the half wave equal to the negative peaks, with R45 holding it about 0.7 V below 0 V; Q15 and R50 turn that into the current U4 amplifies through the Darlington pair Q11/Q12. §5-21 step 13 calls the same trace the positive peaks. Whichever way round the sign is described, what the step is testing is that a half wave appears here at all.",
