   "note": "Scope point, described as a waveform. §2-161: U3A creates the half wave equal to the positive peaks of the H4 signal, with R47 holding it about 0.7 V above 0 V, and Q16 with R48 turn it into the current U5 amplifies through Q13/Q14. In the dc current function only one of the two halves is ever active -- outputting positive current makes the H4 voltage negative, so U3A's output sits at zero -- which is why a dc-only fault can leave one of these two traces looking dead and be perfectly correct.",
